# Party banter on Yester Hill. Each node opens with an `if` gate.

~ banter_humming
if not flag.yester_hill_resolved
interject name:silvain_aster: Listen to it. One note, held for days, by people taking turns. It's a ritual of attrition. Fascinating. Horrible, but fascinating.
interject name:ilse_varga: How many of them?
interject name:silvain_aster: Enough to take turns.
endif
-> END

~ banter_effigy
if flag.yester_hill_known and not flag.yester_hill_resolved
interject tag:cheerful: A forty-foot statue of the man in the castle, made of mud. Does he know? Do you think he's flattered?
interject tag:devout: Mm. Men like him are always flattered. That's the weak joint in them.
endif
-> END

~ banter_after_the_hill
if flag.yester_hill_resolved and not flag.gulthias_tree_burned
interject tag:blunt: We left the tree.
interject tag:bookish: Trees don't walk. Generally.
interject tag:blunt: Generally.
endif
-> END

~ banter_burned
if flag.gulthias_tree_burned
interject name:hedda_ironvow: I keep hearing it. The sound it made. I'll pray for it tonight, and I don't know who I'll be praying for.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Pray for the next person who'd have climbed that hill. That's who.
endif
-> END

~ banter_elvir
if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled
interject name:ilse_varga: "I told him fly." He gave the order and took the cost. That's command. Most officers never learn it.
interject tag:curious: Then we tell his father. Today.
endif
-> END
